# Tailwind — scale classes, no inline styling

## Prefer scale utilities

Use Tailwind’s built-in spacing, type, and tracking scale. Avoid arbitrary values like `text-[0.78rem]` or `mt-[0.35rem]` when a named utility is close enough.

**Prefer**

- `text-xs` / `text-sm` / `text-base` / `text-lg` over `text-[0.78rem]`
- `mt-1` / `mt-1.5` / `mt-2` over `mt-[0.35rem]`
- `px-3` `py-2` / `p-4` over `p-[1.15rem_1.2rem]`
- `tracking-wide` / `tracking-wider` / `tracking-widest` over `tracking-[0.08em]`
- `gap-2` / `gap-3` / `gap-4` over `gap-[0.65rem]`
- Responsive type: `text-4xl md:text-5xl` over `text-[clamp(...)]`

**Allowed exceptions** (only when the scale cannot express the layout)

- One-off layout math: `w-[min(920px,calc(100%-2rem))]`
- Complex grids with no scale equivalent: `grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(...))]`

## No inline styling

Do not style from the template with runtime width/color math.

- No `style=""` / `[style.*]` / `[style.width]`
- No template `Map.get(...)` or method calls that pick CSS classes for layout
- Derive presentation fields in a `computed` (e.g. `widthClass` on each row) and bind with `[ngClass]="row.widthClass"`
- Prefer static Tailwind classes; use `[ngClass]` only for discrete state (ok/error) or precomputed utility names

Wrong:

```html
<div [style.width.%]="percent(row)"></div>
<div [ngClass]="barWidthByLabel().get(row.label) ?? 'w-1/6'"></div>
```

Right:

```ts
// in computed rankRows
widthClass: widthClassForRatio(row.revenue / max)
```

```html
<div class="h-full bg-accent" [ngClass]="row.widthClass"></div>
```
